\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =3{x}^{2}+1 \\\\ f(3) & =3(3)^{2}+1 \\\\  & =27+1 \\\\  & =28\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(3)=28.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485499 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078532 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3b2229bd-c425-5e53-b8cf-56f3f9f3f539" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Polynomial Using Function Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bf881b2-13e8-5a22-ae7e-ec683fc8ab04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484906} {:answer/id #uuid "51fefe0c-6917-5f99-be00-78bf52de691d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484997} {:answer/id #uuid "57e8cf6d-8d35-5805-8a29-824f9a26363b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485015} {:answer/id #uuid "60d844b9-8ae4-59d2-a8d1-c0bdccdc4cff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485032} {:answer/id #uuid "84297f1f-e6e8-5683-af04-f7b713873948" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485101}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2bf881b2-13e8-5a22-ae7e-ec683fc8ab04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484906} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f6bd22d-0ba9-56fb-9f12-08c0ea8052b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485426}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "14cc1a32-5526-5826-8d11-3b9752e2a607" :question/math-academy-id "q-74463" :question/problem "Given the polynomial $g(x)={x}^{4}+3{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-4x,$ $g(1)=$" :question/worked-solution "We substitute $x=1$ into the expression for $g(x)$ and simplify: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(x) & ={x}^{4}+3{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-4x \\\\ g(1) & ={1}^{4}+3\\cdot {1}^{3}+{1}^{2}-4\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1+3+1-4 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(1)=1.$"}]}
